From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Flax <hmccanne@exclamationpoint.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Keep IPMI manual fan mode and duty across reboots and swampd
 restarts

Manual mode set with the OEM fan control command (NetFn 0x2E, IANA 49871,
cmd 0x04, subcommand 1) lived only in swampd's memory, and the duty set with
subcommand 3 was just the FanPwm Target property, which swampd overwrites as
soon as it is back in automatic mode.  A BMC reboot, a swampd restart, or
swampd's in-process zone rebuild on an entity-manager config change all
silently handed the fans back to the PID loop.

The IPMI handler now records the state in
/var/lib/phosphor-pid-control/manual-zone<N>: the file exists while the zone
is manual and lists "<pwm> <duty>" for each output given a duty in that time.
Turning manual mode off deletes it.  swampd reads it every time it builds its
zones, before their control loops start, and puts back Manual and each
Target.

Restoring in swampd rather than in a oneshot unit is deliberate: a config
change rebuilds the zones without restarting the service, and a unit ordered
after phosphor-pid-control.service would never see that.

Only changes made over IPMI are recorded; a busctl write to Manual or Target
is not.  /var is the rwfs overlay, so a factory reset clears the state.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [platform-specific]

---
--- a/ipmi/manualcmds.cpp
+++ b/ipmi/manualcmds.cpp
@@ -19,6 +19,7 @@
 #include "control.hpp"
 #include "dbus_mode.hpp"
 #include "manual_messages.hpp"
+#include "manual_persist.hpp"
 
 #include <ipmid/api.h>
 
@@ -120,6 +121,27 @@
     /* 0 is false, 1 is true */
     ipmi_ret_t rc = _control->setFanCtrlProperty(
         request->zone, static_cast<bool>(request->value), manualProperty);
+    if (rc)
+    {
+        return rc;
+    }
+
+    /*
+     * Remember the mode so swampd puts it back after a reboot or restart.
+     * Entering manual again keeps any duties already recorded; leaving it
+     * forgets the zone entirely.
+     */
+    if (request->value)
+    {
+        auto duties = manual_persist::load(request->zone)
+                          .value_or(manual_persist::Duties{});
+        manual_persist::save(request->zone, duties);
+    }
+    else
+    {
+        manual_persist::clear(request->zone);
+    }
+
     return rc;
 }
 
@@ -153,9 +175,26 @@
     /* This command carries no response payload. */
     *dataLen = 0;
 
+    /*
+     * A duty is only remembered while the zone is manual: in automatic mode
+     * swampd overwrites it on its next cycle, so there is nothing to restore.
+     */
+    manual_persist::Duties duties;
+    if (manual)
+    {
+        duties = manual_persist::load(request->zone)
+                     .value_or(manual_persist::Duties{});
+    }
+
     if (request->fan != allFanPwm)
     {
-        return _control->setFanPwm(request->fan, request->value);
+        rc = _control->setFanPwm(request->fan, request->value);
+        if (rc == IPMI_CC_OK && manual)
+        {
+            duties[request->fan] = request->value;
+            manual_persist::save(request->zone, duties);
+        }
+        return rc;
     }
 
     /* Succeed if at least one PWM output accepted the write. */
@@ -165,9 +204,15 @@
